  ],
  "content": "When dispatching actions in an editor, the second argument to `dispatch` is an `onErrors` callback invoked with any errors thrown by reducers processing the actions. This pattern supports displaying error messages to users, logging errors for debugging, and triggering recovery actions. Example: `dispatch(addTodoItem({ text }), (errors) => { alert(errors[0]?.message); });`\n\nThere is also a **third** parameter the note previously omitted. The full signature (`packages/reactor-browser/src/hooks/dispatch.ts:30-34`) is:\n\n```typescript\ndispatch(\n  actionOrActions: TAction[] | TAction | undefined,\n  onErrors?: (errors: Error[]) => void,\n  onSuccess?: (result: PHDocument) => void,\n)\n```\n\n`onSuccess` receives the updated `PHDocument` once the operation lands. Both callbacks are dispatched by `dispatchActions`, so neither fires when the call bails out before producing a result.\n\n_Source-verified 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse source at v6.2.2-dev.45._",
